## Context
Prose review panel 2026-06-11 (pre-arXiv), convergent factual findings that
block submission. Each needs a fact check against project records, then a
small prose fix.

1. **Wikipedia seeding attribution inconsistency.** Line ~97 says an intern
   injected the content; the COI statement says the author authored several
   pages. Make consistent — the seeded-recall bar's integrity depends on it.
   Related: seeded-recall framing is well-supported only for the built fleet;
   over-extrapolated to all 177 plants in abstract/conclusion.
2. **GEM "119 distinct plants" vs "157 of 177 matched" irreconcilable as
   written** (157 > 119). Explain (snapshot difference?) or correct. Also:
   pin the GEM release version (provenance emphasis demands it).
3. **"All produced usable tables" is false.** GPT-5.5 declined 3/5 reps,
   scored F1=0. Reword: "all yielded a scored outcome (including three
   refusals scored F1=0)"; report GPT-5.5's conditional F1 on its 2 completing
   runs alongside the refusal rate.

